<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad I of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1081–1110</span> · Also known as Conrad of Wirtemberg, Konrad von Beutelsbach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad of Wirtemberg is the first known lord of Württemberg, recorded between 1081 and 1110. He built the castle on the Wirtemberg hill above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a>, from which the dynasty and later the state took their name. He is regarded as the ancestor of the house of Württemberg, although the exact link to the later counts is uncertain.</p></div>
